  "fashion": {
    "Overview": "Neofolk fashion avoids the theatricality of Goth in favor of a disciplined, uniform-based look that combines military surplus with the plainer dress of early-to-mid-20th-century intellectual life. Standard attire includes field jackets in olive drab or field grey, combat boots, and military-grade canvas bags, often paired with turnleneck sweaters, double-breasted trench coats, and high-waisted trousers styled after early 20th-century philosophers and soldiers. Accessories are minimal: silver or iron runic jewelry, and historical military insignia such as the Totenkopf, worn deliberately to provoke a reaction rather than for decoration."
  },
